; example.com. zone for Phase 5 (zone walking).
; Two names are advertised (example.com, www). The rest are internal service
; hostnames that appear nowhere public. The whole point of the phase is that an
; NSEC-signed zone still lets an attacker recover these hidden names.
$TTL 3600
example.com.        IN  SOA ns.example.com. admin.example.com. (
                            2026102301 3600 1800 604800 3600 )
example.com.        IN  NS  ns.example.com.
ns.example.com.     IN  A   172.16.3.30

; advertised
example.com.        IN  A   172.16.1.20
www.example.com.    IN  A   172.16.1.20

; internal / not advertised anywhere
backup.example.com.   IN  A   10.0.0.5
dev.example.com.      IN  A   10.0.0.6
git.example.com.      IN  A   10.0.0.7
mail.example.com.     IN  A   10.0.0.8
staging.example.com.  IN  A   10.0.0.9
vpn.example.com.      IN  A   10.0.0.10
